  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "If\n\n\\[ \\begin{aligned} (7+4\\sqrt3)x^2 &+(2+\\sqrt3)x\\\\ &-2=0, \\end{aligned} \\]\n\nthe larger root minus the smaller root is:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(-2+3\\sqrt3\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(2-\\sqrt3\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(6+3\\sqrt3\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(6-3\\sqrt3\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(3\\sqrt3+2\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "d",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1964-p30.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Let \\(A=7+4\\sqrt3=(2+\\sqrt3)^2\\) and \\(B=2+\\sqrt3.\\) The discriminant is \\[B^2-4A(-2)=A+8A=9A.\\] Hence the root difference is \\[\\frac{\\sqrt{9A}}A=\\frac3{2+\\sqrt3}=6-3\\sqrt3.\\]\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D.",
      "hints": [
        "Notice that \\(7+4\\sqrt3=(2+\\sqrt3)^2\\)",
        "For \\(Ax^2+Bx+C=0,\\) the root difference is \\(\\frac{\\sqrt{B^2-4AC}}{A}\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
